WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Module review · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Recap: Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Before you launch, check that your legal duties, policies and risks each have an owner.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
You built your legal and compliance framework before launch: a map of your duties, the policies you actually need, contract checks, usable procedures, safe reporting channels and a risk register with clear owners.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
One lesson at a time

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:38.511
10.1 Your legal and regulatory map: Your legal duties come from your form, activities and locations, and from your first funders, customers or partners.

6
00:00:38.511 --> 00:00:49.370
10.2 Working out which policies you actually need: A new organisation needs fewer policies than you might think, and copied policies nobody follows create risks.

7
00:00:49.370 --> 00:01:00.119
10.3 Contracts and agreements: You will sign contracts before you are fully set up, so a register and pre-signature checks protect you.

8
00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:01.119
One lesson at a time

9
00:01:01.119 --> 00:01:11.978
10.4 Core policies: conduct, conflicts and anti-fraud: A small core of conduct, conflict of interest and anti-fraud policies is easiest to write before habits form.

10
00:01:11.978 --> 00:01:20.615
10.5 Safeguarding: Safeguarding applies from your very first activity or pilot, including online and in the stories you share.

11
00:01:20.615 --> 00:01:31.733
10.6 Data protection and privacy: Data protection applies from the first sign-up: collect only what you need, keep it secure and be open.

12
00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:32.733
One lesson at a time

13
00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:43.222
10.7 Whistleblowing, complaints and incident reporting: In a small team, a safe route to raise concerns with someone outside the founders is especially important.

14
00:01:43.222 --> 00:01:51.859
10.8 HR and workplace policies: As soon as you engage anyone, even one volunteer, you need some workplace policies.

15
00:01:51.859 --> 00:02:01.867
10.9 Writing usable procedures: Every important policy needs a usable procedure, even if only you carry out the task today.

16
00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:02.867
One lesson at a time

17
00:02:02.867 --> 00:02:12.244
10.10 Policy management and review: Policies only protect people when they are approved, known, followed and reviewed through a simple cycle.

18
00:02:12.244 --> 00:02:22.363
10.11 Identifying and assessing risk: Describing each risk as cause, event and consequence lets your response target the cause or soften the impact.

19
00:02:22.363 --> 00:02:33.481
10.12 Risk registers, ownership, mitigation and escalation: A short risk register with owners, actions and escalation rules is one you will actually use.

20
00:02:33.881 --> 00:02:34.481
One lesson at a time

21
00:02:34.481 --> 00:02:44.489
10.13 Monitoring and reviewing risk: Early risks change quickly, so regular reviews and early warning signs keep the register alive.

22
00:02:45.089 --> 00:02:57.689
Every foundation is now in place. Bring it all together, retake your health check against your starting point and review your foundations regularly as your initiative grows.

23
00:02:58.289 --> 00:03:03.089
You check your Compliance & Risk Pack and download each exercise as a PDF.

24
00:03:04.589 --> 00:03:07.689
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
